# Text input

Use a labelled input for a short answer on one line.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it for a room name, a display label or a known identifier. Match the width to the expected answer where that helps, while allowing the control to shrink to its container.

## When not to use it

Do not use placeholder text as the label or force a paragraph into a one-line field. Avoid number inputs for codes with leading zeros.

## Home Assistant adaptation

Use friendly names for ordinary household tasks; show entity identifiers only when the task requires them. For measurements, state the unit in the label as well as any visual suffix. Accept sensible formatting instead of rejecting an answer solely for harmless spaces.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Associate a persistent label, hint and any error. Choose an appropriate input mode without changing the underlying meaning of the value. Keep copy and paste available. Use personal-data autocomplete only when the field actually requests that personal information.

